A.In SAP Cloud Platform Integration (CPI), CPI, API Management, Open Connectors, Trading Partner Management,
  and Integration Advisor are key components of the SAP Integration Suite that facilitate the integration of
  SAP and non-SAP systems. CPI is the core platform for connecting these systems, while the others are specialized
  capabilities that enhance and streamline the integration process.

  CPI (Cloud Platform Integration):
  This is the foundational platform within SAP Integration Suite, enabling connectivity between SAP and non-SAP
  cloud and on-premise applications. It serves as the middleware for data exchange and process orchestration.

  API Management:
  This capability allows for the creation, publication, and governance of APIs (Application Programming Interfaces).
  It enables secure and scalable access to digital assets, promoting coinnovation among employees, partners, and
  the developer community.

  Open Connectors:
  These are pre-built, standardized connectors that simplify integration with numerous third-party applications
  and services, including popular SaaS applications. They provide normalized authentication, error handling,
  and connectivity mechanisms, making integration faster and easier.

  Trading Partner Management (TPM):
  This capability manages business-to-business (B2B) interactions with external trading partners, streamlining
  the management of B2B relationships, agreements, and data exchange. It helps define and configure electronic
  data interchange protocols and standards for each trading partner.

  Integration Advisor:
  This tool provides a crowdsources, machine-learning approach to solving B2B, application-to-application (A2A),
  and business-to-government (B2G) integration scenarios. It helps accelerate the development of business-oriented
  interfaces and mappings, reducing development efforts